{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nAn AST inventory finds 110 broad environment constructions under tests: 51 `dict(os.environ)`, 49 `{**os.environ, ...}`, and 10 `os.environ.copy()`. Seven decorated pytest fixtures are owned by sibling `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran`, leaving exactly 103 test-local/helper sites here. A real pytest runtime probe proved that when process startup raises, default long tracebacks render ordinary environment mappings through `subprocess.run`, `Popen`, and `_execute_child`, exposing early inherited values; short tracebacks do not. A late sentinel can be truncated, so absence without insertion-order control is not proof. Production and maintenance propagation remain excluded.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a test-only mutable dict boundary whose representation redacts contents, whose mapping behavior preserves exact inherited child environments, and whose `.copy()` preserves the boundary.\n- Route all 103 non-fixture broad constructions through that boundary; retain every key/value/order and per-test override so intentional ambient propagation remains behaviorally unchanged.\n- Add a real nested-pytest startup-failure oracle using an existing production-path helper, with a first-position sentinel and short-trace negative control.\n- Add an AST repository-policy guard that recognizes the three inventoried broad forms, skips the seven separately-owned decorated fixtures, permits only the single boundary constructor, rejects unclassified new broad mappings, and rejects `dict(...)` unwrapping of the boundary.\n- Verify the exact child environment reaches a successful subprocess, the guard catches seeded new constructions/unwrapping, all affected test files collect and run, and focused/full gates pass.\n\n## Test contract card\n- authoritative_contract: failure-output non-disclosure at `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py:13-45` and commit 034e17209c.\n- trigger_preconditions: sentinel is first in the parent mapping; a real subprocess startup fails before returning.\n- production_path: existing `tests/integration/test_init_fail_closed.py::_env` -> real `subprocess.run` -> pytest long traceback.\n- test_tier: nested real pytest + real subprocess; a pure repr unit test cannot cross pytest/stdlib frame rendering.\n- observable_postcondition: long and short captured output omit the sentinel; successful child receives the exact value.\n- negative_control: the short traceback never renders the sentinel.\n- ci_gate: `make test` / unit repository-policy lane.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every one of the 103 in-scope broad mappings uses the representation-safe boundary; the seven decorated fixtures remain owned by their sibling ticket.\n- [ ] A first-position sentinel is absent from default-long and short exception-time traceback probes.\n- [ ] A successful child receives exact inherited values and intentional ambient-propagation behavior remains unchanged.\n- [ ] A repository AST guard rejects each raw broad-construction form and boundary unwrapping, citing the offending location.\n- [ ] Focused suites, lint, typecheck, and the complete supported test gate pass.\n- [ ] The exact ordinary-dict mutation returns the held-out security oracle to RED."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787034558733305001,"uuid":"b6813ae9-fb89-4f31-a584-ad95e2dc7755"}